46    write(11, "The skill loaded successfully. Applying its workflow to the dummy scenario (I've already read both reference files):\n\n**Skill output for the `DummyNotes` dummy scenario:**\n\n**Recommended navigation pattern**\n- A **single primary stack** for Notes (list \342\206\222 note detail \342\206\222 attachment viewer, ~3 levels), with **Search** integrated into that stack/top bar rather than a separate tab.\n- **Settings** reached via a button/sheet, not a tab.\n- **New note** and **Filter/sort** as **modals/sheets** (sheet for filter, modal or sheet for quick entry).\n- On **iPad**, use a **split view** (notes list as sidebar, detail as the secondary pane).\n- Map `dummynotes://note/dummy-id` into the Notes stack so the back stack stays intact (list \342\206\222 detail).\n\n**Rationale**\nThe app has one dominant flow (notes) used constantly while Settings is rare, so the decision tree favors a focused stack over tabs; short self-contained tasks (new note, filter) fit modals/sheets, and split view improves iPad side-by-side context.\n\n**Risks / trade-offs (validated against anti-patterns)**\n- Avoid making Settings a tab \342\200\224 it's used rarely (anti-pattern: \"tabs for sections used rarely\").\n- Keep the new-note + filter sheets from stacking on top of each other (anti-pattern: \"multiple stacked modals\").\n- Ensure the deep link rebuilds the back stack rather than presenting the note modally with a broken back path.\n- Depth stays at ~3 levels, well within the 4\342\200\2235 level guideline.\n\nThe skill executed end-to-end. Here is the structured execution summary.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"skill_name\": \"ios-navigation-architecture\",\n  \"documented_purpose\": \"Choose and review iOS navigation patterns (tabs, stacks, modals, sheets, deep links) for designing app structure or refactoring navigation. Platform guidance only, not implementation.\",\n  \"files_inspected\": [\n    \"/home/appuser/.claude/skills/ios-navigation-architecture/SKILL.md\",\n    \"/home/appuser/.claude/skills/ios-navigation-architecture/references/anti-patterns.md\",\n    \"/home/a"..., 4029) = 4029
